  "inheritanceChain": ["Titanium.UI.View", "Titanium.Proxy"],
  "platforms": ["iphone", "ipad", "macos"],
  "since": {
    "iphone": "0.8",
    "ipad": "0.8",
    "macos": "9.2.0"
  },
  "summary": "The cover flow view is a container showing animated three-dimensional images in a style \nconsistent with the former cover flow presentation style used for iPod, iTunes, and Finder.\n",
  "description": "The cover flow view is created by the [Titanium.UI.iOS.createCoverFlowView](api:Titanium.UI.iOS#createCoverFlowView) method or \n**`<CoverFlowView>`** element in an Alloy application.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Simple 3 image cover flow example",
      "code": "Create a simple cover flow view.\n\n``` js\nvar view = Titanium.UI.iOS.createCoverFlowView({\n  backgroundColor:'#000',\n  images:['a.png','b.png','c.png']\n});\nwindow.add(view);\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alloy XML Markup",
      "code": "Previous example as an Alloy view.\n\n``` xml\n<Alloy>\n    <Window id=\"window\">\n        <CoverFlowView id=\"view\" platform=\"ios\" backgroundColor=\"#000\">\n\n            <!-- The Images tag sets the CoverFlowView.images property. -->\n            <Images>\n\n                <!-- Assign the image by node text or the image attribute. -->\n                <!-- Can also specify the width and height attributes. -->\n\n                <Image>a.png</Image>\n                <Image>b.png</Image>\n                <Image>c.png</Image>\n\n            </Images>\n\n            <!-- Place additional views for the CoverFlowView here. -->\n\n        </CoverFlowView>\n    </Window>\n</Alloy>\n```\n"
    }
  ],
